          {
            "id": "s1:p1",
            "text": "Carex panicea, commonly known as carnation sedge, is a plant species in the sedge family, Cyperaceae. It is known as grass-like sedge and can be found in Northern and Western Europe, and also in north-eastern North America. The plant produces fruits which are {{convert|3|-|4|mm}} long, are egg shaped and spiked. Both male and female species leaves are pale blue on both sides."
          }
